From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:43:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Look line breaks up in a table

`analyze_text` finds the line break opportunities of a text under the
default rules in a table (`parley_engine`'s `line_table.rs`), for characters
up to U+017F and from U+2000 to U+203F, as UAX #14's pair table does.

The table is what ICU4X's line segmenter gives. A test generates it, fails
when the table is out of date and prints it anew. A word with a character
outside the table (an inline object's among them), or a pair that changes
with the characters around it, is given to ICU4X with the words on either
side. A debug build gives every text looked up to ICU4X whole too, and
compares.

`AnalysisOptions::skip_word_boundaries`
(`LayoutContext::set_word_boundaries`, on by default) leaves word boundaries
out, for text no one moves through by words with the layout's clusters.
